v0.2.15 - child ctx inside inject, startup-timing fix, silent-failure audit

Two further issues found by auditing every silent-failure mode rather than
just the last one:

1. Config-page registration used the parent ctx's slots/effect while running
   inside a ctx.inject child plugin. Official dsh-context uses the child ctx;
   ctx.effect asserts the fiber is active, and the whileServed callback can
   fire after apply returns. Now uses scoped.slots / scoped.effect.

2. The settings service was captured once at startup. ctx.get() is strict and
   returns undefined when the service fiber is not yet ready, without
   throwing - so a later-arriving service was dropped permanently and slash
   command config writes would fail forever. Now looked up per call.

Adds scripts/verify-client-contract.mjs, which asserts every silent failure
mode hit in recent rounds: exports["./client"], minimal top-level inject,
remote + remote.settings requested together, slot name and key, locale
dictionary, no ctx access in the render path, and the built bundle containing
the registration.

311 tests.
